Worker message interface
==========================

The FastStream worker exposes a message interface that downstream services
integrate against: it consumes :class:`~{{github_repo_name}}.worker.app.VersionRequest`
on the ``version-requests`` destination and publishes
:class:`~{{github_repo_name}}.worker.app.VersionResponse` on ``version-responses``,
over {{worker_broker}}.

The `AsyncAPI <https://www.asyncapi.com/>`_ specification below is the
machine-readable contract for that interface — the channels, payload schemas,
and broker binding. It is generated on every docs build directly from the live
``{{github_repo_name}}.worker.app:app`` object (via ``faststream docs gen``), so
it stays in lockstep with the code and the ``description=`` strings on the
subscriber and publisher.

.. literalinclude:: _generated/asyncapi.yaml
   :language: yaml
   :caption: asyncapi.yaml

.. note::

   To regenerate the schema locally outside a docs build:

   .. code-block:: console

      $ uv run --group docs faststream docs gen --yaml \
          {{github_repo_name}}.worker.app:app --out docs/_generated/asyncapi.yaml
